    "title": "Police identify victim in fatal Bernalillo shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "BERNALILLO, N.M. (KRQE) – KRQE News 13 has learned more about a deadly shooting in Bernalillo that left one dead and another injured. The victim who was shot and killed has been identified as 27-year-old Joshua Williams. Police are still searching for the suspect who was described as being 6-foot tall, wearing a purple shirt, and a black ski mask. Anyone with information on the shooting is encouraged to contact the Bernalillo Police Department. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRQE NEWS 13 - Breaking News, Albuquerque News, New Mexico News, Weather, and Videos.",
